body: "## Observed failure (hosted CI, not a new local reproduction)\n\nAt PR #24 head `d7f1e61b6d90add7ed2d61bc570278398f302198`, both Node 22 and Node 26 fail the existing test **“start refuses terminal lanes and rolls back newly acquired claims on Git or field failures”**, at `test/edges.test.ts:28:10`: expected `false`, actual `true`.\n\n- [Node 22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40462648873/job/122050615194)\n- [Node 26 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40462648873/job/122050615276)\n- [Exact test](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/d7f1e61b6d90add7ed2d61bc570278398f302198/test/edges.test.ts#L9-L29)\n\nThe Node 22 run reports 555 tests, 554 passing, 1 failing. This is the outer suite failure, not intentionally failing nested fixtures printed by tooling tests.\n\n## Reproduction / expected behavior\n\nUse the repository’s existing fixture and linked SDK setup, then run:\n\n```sh\nnode --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"start refuses terminal lanes\" test/edges.test.ts\n```\n\nThe test creates a `PmClient({cwd, pmRoot, author:'swarm-test', noExtensions:true})`. After releasing the prior claim, `Swarm.start(id)` rejects, but a subsequent read still reports `claim_state.claimed === true`.\n\nExpected: an unsuccessful start must release a claim newly acquired by that attempt. It must retain a pre-existing claim, and preserve genuinely intervening peer changes. Actual: the newly acquired claim remains held after the rejected start.\n\nImpact: a caller receives a failed start with no usable lane while leaving the item assigned/claimed, potentially blocking another agent’s work.\n\n## Static lead, not a proven root cause\n\n[Current start cleanup/admission](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/d7f1e61b6d90add7ed2d61bc570278398f302198/src/swarm.ts#L147-L195) initializes `claimVersion` from the pre-claim version and advances it only in `onCommitted`; cleanup then uses that version in `releaseAcquiredClaim`. Check whether the no-extensions path supplies the same committed-document/version evidence before applying the stale-document guard. This is an inspection lead; the evidence above establishes the observable leak, not its complete causal chain.\n\n## Canonical scope and deduplication\n\nThe existing [pm-swarm-y972 item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/d7f1e61b6d90add7ed2d61bc570278398f302198/.agents/pm/features/pm-swarm-y972.toon) already includes this edge-test command and cleanup-preservation work. All-status issues and the current PM feature corpus were checked. This is distinct from #27’s close-after-handoff/reclaim refusal: this failure occurs during failed **start**, with a newly acquired claim.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n\n- The named existing test passes on Node 22 and Node 26, including both newly acquired and pre-existing claim cases.\n- A rejected start leaves no newly owned claim, lane, or Git branch behind.\n- Cleanup retains generation/document fencing: do not release a peer’s replacement claim or overwrite intervening content to make the test pass.\n- The no-extensions refusal remains truthful; do not silently enable extensions.\n- Re-run the existing acquisition-receipt/start-cleanup/peer-cleanup suites and full release gate, recording any remaining gaps.\n\nLimits: this report relies on exact-head hosted test evidence plus static source analysis. No destructive, crash, permission, or concurrency fault-injection drills were run locally; no whole-release certification is implied.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (4)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-10-27T07:03:14Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-swarm#12 - Renew shared tracker leases with fencing, reclaim and handoff [merged]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-27T08:53:38Z)\n>\n> Verified follow-up on PR #24 head `b8f9bb7121c586b7479fc502b1e143db220e1209` (2026-10-27).\n> \n> The reported failed-start claim leak is addressed in this head: `requireActiveExtensionRead` checks request-local hook activation before `start` acquires the native claim, and the original `edges.test.ts` newly acquired/pre-existing claim assertions remain present and pass. The added start/next/schedule cases also require unchanged durable tracker/history/liveness and no Git branch for an inactive client.\n> \n> Hosted evidence:\n> - [Node 22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40466517792/job/122063124413)\n> - [Node 26 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40466517792/job/122063124685)\n> \n> Both gates succeed with 564 functional tests, 100% aggregate coverage and four packed acceptance checks. The previously failing named start/rollback test explicitly passes in both logs. Six additional bounded, exact-source mocked checks of the new request-local activation helper pass on Node 24.22.1, including inactive refusal, active result preservation, non-leaking outside-context reads, original error propagation, and independent asynchronous scopes.\n> \n> [Exact guard](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/b8f9bb7121c586b7479fc502b1e143db220e1209/src/settings.ts), [call before acquisition](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/b8f9bb7121c586b7479fc502b1e143db220e1209/src/swarm.ts), [regressions](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/b8f9bb7121c586b7479fc502b1e143db220e1209/test/start-admission-race.test.ts).\n> \n> Limits: PR remains open/unmerged at this check; this is not evidence of a published artifact fix. Local checks mocked SDK/filesystem dependencies and did not repeat real concurrency, crash or Git mutation drills. No issue closure or whole-release certification implied.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-27T14:30:27Z)\n>\n> Final-head CI gap for the existing start/cleanup acceptance (not a recurrence claim for the original noExtensions leak).\n> \n> At PR #24 head `3e51e708e8b1ca20effa68a1da9c9d5fe5eb9954`, both [Node 22](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40504674653/job/122190829706) and [Node 26](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40504674653/job/122190830105) finish with 750 tests, 745 passing and five failing; aggregate branch coverage is 99.91%.\n> \n> The failures establish a contract/assertion conflict, not unsafe peer overwrite:\n> - reservation-cleanup.test.ts:47, start-cleanup.test.ts:55 and start-peer-cleanup.test.ts:64 reject the current `swarm_superseded` result because their validators expect an earlier generic cleanup error/category.\n> - The publication and rollback cases in [review-r9.test.ts:52–68](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/3e51e708e8b1ca20effa68a1da9c9d5fe5eb9954/test/review-r9.test.ts#L52-L68) reach the branch-removal assertion at line65 with actual true, expected false. Their preceding unchanged-assignee and history-count assertions pass. Current cleanup now rechecks ownership under the native item lock and refuses cleanup after supersession.\n> \n> The accepted round4 record in [pm-swarm-y972](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/3e51e708e8b1ca20effa68a1da9c9d5fe5eb9954/.agents/pm/features/pm-swarm-y972.toon) explicitly requires preserving peer native-history transitions as `swarm_superseded`. Its last receipt still says full hosted admission was unavailable; these terminal jobs now establish the remaining gate gap.\n> \n> Please reconcile the old assertions with the intended typed refusal/resource-preservation contract rather than weakening native-history fencing to make them pass. Acceptance: verify exact item/history/Git-resource preservation before checking errors, retain negative controls and original noExtensions coverage, and pass the full final-head Node22/26 and packed/Bun gates with unchanged coverage thresholds. The prior b8f9bb7 fix evidence remains scoped to that revision.\n> \n> Limits: this follow-up independently inspects hosted logs and immutable source, not a new local concurrency/crash run or published-artifact certification. All-status repository issues and the current canonical record/comments were checked; this extends the existing cleanup-suite acceptance instead of opening a duplicate.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-02T09:26:55Z)\n>\n> Fixed on main. Evidence: PR #24 merged 2026-10-29T02:44Z (3ee1ad5): start gates claim acquisition on request-local hook activation, so a failed start releases its newly acquired claim; edges.test.ts claim assertions pass; main CI success run 41303369670 (2026-11-01T11:46Z) (Found in the 2026-11-02 triage of issues the blind issue watch missed.)"
